      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the perimeter of the larger triangle, we first need to determine the scale factor between the two triangles. Since the triangles are similar, the ratio of their corresponding sides is the same.\n\nThe ratio of the longest sides of the triangles is $\\frac{10}{25} = \\frac{2}{5}$.\n\nSince the triangles are isosceles, the other two sides of the larger triangle are also scaled by the same factor. So, the other two sides of the larger triangle are each $\\frac{2}{5} \\times 8 = \\frac{16}{5}$ cm.\n\nNow, we can find the perimeter of the larger triangle by adding up the lengths of all three sides:\n\n$\\frac{16}{5} + \\frac{16}{5} + 25 = \\frac{32}{5} + 25 = \\frac{32}{5} + \\frac{125}{5} = \\frac{157}{5} = \\boxed{31.4}$ cm.\n\nThe perimeter of the larger triangle is $\\boxed{31.4}$ centimeters.\nThe answer is: 31.4",
