      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to understand the concept of similar triangles. Two triangles are similar if their corresponding angles are equal and their corresponding sides are proportional. In this case, the triangles are similar because they have two sides of equal length and the longest side of the larger triangle is a multiple of the longest side of the smaller triangle.\n\nGiven that the longest side of the smaller triangle is 10 cm and the longest side of the larger triangle is 25 cm, we can set up a proportion to find the scale factor between the two triangles. The scale factor is the ratio of the longest sides of the larger and smaller triangles:\n\nScale factor = 25 cm / 10 cm = 2.5\n\nNow that we have the scale factor, we can find the lengths of the other sides of the larger triangle by multiplying the corresponding sides of the smaller triangle by the scale factor:\n\nSide 1 of larger triangle = 8 cm * 2.5 = 20 cm\nSide 2 of larger triangle = 8 cm * 2.5 = 20 cm\nSide 3 of larger triangle = 10 cm * 2.5 = 25 cm\n\nFinally, we can find the perimeter of the larger triangle by adding up all its sides:\n\nPerimeter of larger triangle = 20 cm + 20 cm + 25 cm = 65 cm\n\nSo, the perimeter of the larger triangle is 65 cm.",
